{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-torus-knot-genus-four-unique","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:torus-knot-genus-four-unique","kind":"proposition","title":"Genus-$4$ torus knots: $\\{T_{2,9}, T_{3,5}\\}$ are the only solutions","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-torus-knot-generators"],"tags":["torus-knot","genus-4","diophantine","uniqueness","number-theoretic"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Archimedean.torus_knot_genus_four_unique","text":"torus-knot-genus-four-unique.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:torus-knot-genus-four-unique\"></a><p><em>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">g \\in \\mathbb{Z}_{\\geq 0}</code>. Consider torus knots <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_{m,n}</code> with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2 \\leq m \\leq n</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\gcd(m, n) = 1</code>. The genus is <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">g(T_{m,n}) = (m-1)(n-1)/2</code> (<a href=\"#prop:torus-knot-generators\" data-at=\"brings-surface/archimedean-condition-genus-completeness\">torus knot generators</a>). At <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">g = 4</code>, the equation <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(m-1)(n-1) = 8</code> has exactly two positive integer solutions with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">m \\leq n</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\gcd(m, n) = 1</code>:</em></p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Solution</th>\n<th><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(m, n)</code></th>\n<th>crossing number <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">c = m(n-1)</code></th>\n<th><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\gcd(m, n)</code></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(m{-}1,\\, n{-}1) = (1,\\, 8)</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(2,\\, 9)</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">9</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1</code> (yes)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(m{-}1,\\, n{-}1) = (2,\\, 4)</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(3,\\, 5)</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">10</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1</code> (yes)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/torus-knot-genus-four-unique.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"16.5.7","page":"b/prop-torus-knot-genus-four-unique","qa":{"counts":{"pass":88,"fail":1,"warn":0,"na":12,"unknown":0,"stale":74},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.MassTheory.Archimedean.torus_knot_genus_four_unique","via":"ref","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/BraidKnotOctonion/TorusKnotGenusFourUnique.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
